* Every Game Object with its own independent identity is an Entity
* Example: the player is an Entity, his chain weapon is not
* We use one central Entity interface that includes all relevant state, including render/animation/health state
* State that is not relevant to the entity type is null
* Each Entity has a unique ID, we use a counter
* We mark dead entities as dead via bool and keep them instead of removing them, systems skip dead
* We keep different types of entities in different arrays, e.g. buildings, towers, enemies, players
* For each Entity type we have a central manager class that implements update and render methods
* Managers are created in the central Game class and can access each others state through the Game class